/**
 * Contact discovery and the verification cascade.
 *
 * Nothing here invents a person and nothing here invents an address. Contacts
 * come from evidence already in the database — a job description that names a
 * recruiter, an address embedded in a Who's-Hiring post, a mailto on a team
 * page, a LinkedIn row, or something the operator typed. Addresses are either
 * observed the same way, or generated by applying a pattern that was itself
 * inferred from observed addresses at that domain, and then confirmed by a
 * verifier before anyone would email them.
 *
 * The cascade, cheapest first:
 *   free DNS/syntax/role prefilter → domain pattern conformance → paid verifier
 * and every step writes a field_observation carrying the evidence FK it came
 * from, so any value in the UI can be traced back to the document that produced
 * it.
 */

